  "nl_text": "The database named rschema_0411 is used to store information about customers, products, and their purchases. It contains three tables: Customer, Product, and Customer_product_purchase.\nThe Customer table has the following columns: Address, Contact_person, Credit_rating, Customer_ID (primary key), Customer_name, Customer_type, Email, and Phone. The Customer_ID column is an integer and is the primary key. The Address, Contact_person, Credit_rating, Customer_name, Customer_type, Email, and Phone columns are all strings.\nThe Product table has the following columns: Brand, Inventory_quantity, Product_ID (primary key), Product_category, Product_name, Production_date, Specifications, Supplier, and Unit_price. The Product_ID column is an integer and is the primary key. The Brand, Inventory_quantity, Product_category, Product_name, Production_date, Specifications, Supplier, and Unit_price columns are all strings.\nThe Customer_product_purchase table has the following columns: Customer_ID (foreign key), Order_status, Order_time, Payment_method, Payment_status, Payment_time, Product_ID (foreign key), Product_quantity, Total_amount, and Unit_price. The Customer_ID and Product_ID columns are both foreign keys that reference the Customer and Product tables, respectively. The Customer_ID column is not null, and the Product_ID column is not null. The Order_status, Order_time, Payment_method, Payment_status, Payment_time, Product_quantity, Total_amount, and Unit_price columns are all strings. The primary key of the table is a composite of the Customer_ID, Product_ID, and Order_time columns.\nIn summary, the rschema_0411 database stores information about customers, products, and their purchases. It has three tables: Customer, Product, and Customer_product_purchase. Each table has its own set of columns, with the Customer_product_purchase table having foreign keys that reference the Customer and Product tables. The primary keys of the tables are used to ensure data integrity, and the foreign keys are used to enforce referential integrity.",
  "gold_question": "This is a customer management system. For customer management, the system maintains basic customer information (customer ID, customer name, contact person, etc.), records detailed customer information (address, phone, email, etc.), and manages customer classification information (customer type, credit rating). For product management, the system maintains basic product information (product ID, product name, specifications, etc.), records detailed product information (unit price, inventory quantity, production date, etc.), and manages product classification information (product category, brand, supplier, etc.). For purchase management, the system records order information (order time, order status, etc.), maintains order details (product quantity, unit price, total amount, etc.), and manages payment information (payment method, payment status, payment time, etc.).",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_codellama13b/0411.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0411\nCREATE TABLE `customer` (\n  `customer_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `customer_name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `address` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `contact_person` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `credit_rating` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `customer_type` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `email` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `phone` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`customer_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `product` (\n  `product_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `product_name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `brand` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `product_category` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `specifications` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `supplier` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `production_date` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `inventory_quantity` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `unit_price` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`product_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `customer_product_purchase` (\n  `customer_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `product_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `order_time` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `order_status` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `payment_method` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `payment_status` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `payment_time` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `product_quantity` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `total_amount` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `unit_price` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`customer_id`, `product_id`, `order_time`),\n  CONSTRAINT `customer_product_purchase_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`customer_id`) REFERENCES `customer` (`customer_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `customer_product_purchase_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`product_id`) REFERENCES `product` (`product_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
